From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Graham Ollis <plicease@cpan.org>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:46:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Compile under Open Watcom C (large model, Watcom headers)

The smallest changes that let every module compile with wcc -ml against
Open Watcom's own headers. No behaviour change is intended except where
noted.

- perl.h, util.h: hide K&R declarations of time() and setenv() that
  conflict with the ANSI prototypes in Watcom's headers.
- perl.h: declare statstab and statname EXT like their neighbours; without
  it every module defined them, which only a linker with common symbols
  accepts quietly.
- msdos/config.h: no STDSTDIO; Watcom's FILE has no _ptr/_cnt/_base, so
  -T and -B on a filehandle (not a file name) become a fatal error.
- msdos/config.h: STRERROR, from config.h.SH (msdos/config.h predates it);
  Watcom has strerror() but no sys_errlist.
- perly.c: include patchlevel.h, not the 8.3 name patchlev.h.
- toke.c: test YYDEBUG as perl.y does; bison always defines YYDEBUG
  (as 0), which turned on code that needs DEBUGGING.
- cons.c: make_usub() returns a null SUBR* rather than no value.
- eval.c: DOS mkdir() takes no mode; correct the dospatch44 alarm stub's
  message, which said "fork".
- msdos/msdos.c: sleep() returns unsigned, as Watcom declares it; drop a
  getenv() declaration that conflicts with <stdlib.h>.
- msdos/popen.c: atexit() rather than the MSC onexit().
- msdos/directory.c: rejoin an rcsid string split across two lines.
